  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe passive form {報|むく}いられる (to be rewarded) is extremely common, especially in the pattern {努力|どりょく}が{報|むく}いられる (one's efforts are rewarded). The に particle marks what is being repaid: {恩|おん}に{報|むく}いる (repay a kindness), {期待|きたい}に{報|むく}いる (live up to expectations).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {恩|おん}に{報|むく}いる: repay a favor/kindness\n- {期待|きたい}に{報|むく}いる: live up to expectations\n- {努力|どりょく}が{報|むく}いられる: one's efforts are rewarded\n- {仇|あだ}を{報|むく}いる: take revenge\n- {信頼|しんらい}に{報|むく}いる: repay someone's trust\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\nThe related noun {報|むく}い means reward or retribution. {恩返|おんがえ}し (returning a favor) is a noun specifically for repaying kindness. {仕返|しかえ}し (getting back at someone) is more colloquial for revenge.",
